2-Records
:Records are special type of class that help avoid boilerplate code .they are considered "data carriers"
:Records are immutable and are final by default
:you can not extend your custom record because records already (implicitly) extend from the Record class.
this is similar to ENUM(which implicitly extend from Enum)
:Records can have both static filed and static method
:Records can have instance method
:Records can not have instance fields. All the instance field listed as "Components" in the record declaration.
:Records can implement interfaces
:you can override all the default implementations. this include the canonical constructor(perhaps for data validation)

